  "verified_against": {
    "source": "release-manifest.json",
    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.44.0 release assets and hashed independently, then checked again by re-fetching the URL this pin itself names. Only the pegasus artifact changed: install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.28.0 and earlier. v5.44.0 reaches this distribution through the apply_patch plugin it renders under its own name, so it changes what an agent here is told about a tool it always receives. That plugin exists because the tool's description opens with an imperative -- use this tool to edit files -- that a model read as outranking its system prompt, refusing an edit over SSH the person had authorised. It appends a paragraph saying what the tool actually reaches, and it deliberately leaves the runtime's own sentence alone, so that rewording upstream cannot silently switch the correction off. What was missing is the other direction: the paragraph was appended blindly and for ever, so the day upstream fixes that imperative the note becomes text shipped on every call for no reason and nobody learns of it. The plugin now checks whether the sentence it corrects is still there and, when it is not, raises one notice per session rather than one per call. What reaches the model is unchanged. A toast was chosen over a marker file because this distribution already ships a plugin that uses that channel, and because throwing from that hook aborts the turn's tool resolution -- verified in the runtime's source rather than assumed. The guard around it proves the notice fires once even when two calls overlap, which is the shape the runtime really produces, since it caches one hook closure and therefore one flag per directory. Separately, the manual and the installation guide were cut along the line they should have had: the interactive interface and the command surface now live in the manual, the installation guide keeps installing and uninstalling and links to the rest, and one duplication was kept on purpose because the two guides frame the same fact differently for a person and for an agent. This distribution changed nothing of its own for this pin beyond the alignment."
  }
}
